{
  "title": "Bare fruit alternatives before an ambiguous or produce noun still resolve to the fruit",
  "description": "first_alternative lets a bare singular produce word give way to the list's shared noun only when that noun names one non-produce food (\"peach or nectarine jam\" is jam). \
Lines whose shared noun is ambiguous or unknown still count as the fruit: \"lemon or vanilla wafer cookies\" (\"cookies\" is an ambiguous name, so it resolves to lemons), \"apple or pear sauce\" (apples), and \"clementine or orange zest\" (the clementine fruit rather than zest). \
Consider letting an ambiguous shared noun win as Resolution::Ambiguous, and borrowing \"zest\"/\"sauce\" through known compounds (\"orange zest\", \"applesauce\"). \
Measure with make pipeline.",
